\ cv8t-fuse.4 - cv8-fuse.4 under the two-bit tag (Iteration 67, FORMAT-TAG2.md): 64
\ one-byte opcodes and an escape, calls of 2, 3, 4 bytes (14, 22, 30 bits:
\ a 1 GB code space), links of 1-4 bytes. A copy - the original is frozen by
\ the designs recorded with it. The opcode constants keep their logical
\ values here; layout.py --tag2 rewrites each to this design's code.
\ cv8-fuse.4 - the CV8 compiler's fold list and superinstruction pairs
\ as TABLES, which the image converter fills in for each design
\ (tools/layout.py, lab/evolve). Loaded after cv8.4 (and cv8b.4), and
\ only for the designs that need it.
\
\ cv8.4's FOLD-OPS is the default fold list, fixed in the source. A
\ design with a different list - shorter, or in another order - has
\ an engine whose fold opcodes belong to other primitives, so code its
\ compiler folded at RUN time would run the wrong handlers. Here the
\ compiler reads its folds from FOLD-TABLE instead, and fuses pairs of
\ primitives from SUPER-TABLE as it compiles them, as the converter
\ fuses them in the image. The tables' contents below are only
\ defaults: the converter overwrites both in the emitted image.
\
\ Loops are DO guarded by ?DUP IF, not ?DO: the converter does not
\ translate ?DO's inline operand, and DO with equal bounds would run
\ through the whole cell range.
\
\ The X8 words here replace cv8.4's: the converter gives each X the
\ body of the LATEST word named X8.

: FOLD-DEFAULTS ( --- )   #FOLD-OPS 0 DO FOLD-OPS I + C@ C, LOOP ;

CREATE FOLD-TABLE ( --- c-addr )
\ Count, then the folded primitives' opcodes in fold-opcode order.
  #FOLD-OPS C, FOLD-DEFAULTS

CREATE SUPER-TABLE ( --- c-addr )
\ Count, then (first second fused) opcode triples - none by default.
  0 C, 72 ALLOT
ALIGN

: FOLD-OP ( op --- op2 -1 | op 0 )
\ The folded opcode for primitive opcode op, if this design has one.
  FOLD-TABLE C@ ?DUP IF 0 DO
    DUP FOLD-TABLE 1+ I + C@ = IF DROP I FOLD-BASE + -1 UNLOOP EXIT THEN
  LOOP THEN 0 ;

: SUPER-OP ( op1 op2 --- op3 -1 | 0 )
\ The superinstruction for primitive op1 followed by op2, if any.
  SUPER-TABLE C@ ?DUP IF 0 DO
    SUPER-TABLE 1+ I 3 * +
    DUP C@ 3 PICK = OVER 1+ C@ 3 PICK = AND IF
      SWAP DROP SWAP DROP 2 + C@ -1 UNLOOP EXIT
    THEN DROP
  LOOP THEN 2DROP 0 ;

: COMPILE,8 ( xt --- )
\ As cv8.4's, and a primitive compiled straight after another fuses
\ with it when the pair has a superinstruction. LAST-OP must point at
\ the byte just before HERE: anything emitted in between - a call, a
\ literal, an operand - stops the fusion, and anything that makes HERE
\ a branch target clears LAST-OP. The fused byte keeps LAST-OP, and no
\ fold or pair contains a fused opcode, so it never combines again.
  DUP >NAME C@ 32 AND IF
    DUP C@ ESC-OP = IF
      DUP C@ OP, 1+ C@ OP, 0 LAST-OP !
    ELSE
      C@ LAST-OP @ DUP IF DUP 1+ HERE = AND THEN ?DUP IF
        DUP >R C@ OVER SUPER-OP IF SWAP DROP R> C! EXIT THEN R> DROP
      THEN
      HERE LAST-OP ! OP,
    THEN
  ELSE
    CALL,
  THEN ;

: ;8 ( --- )
\ cv8.4's, but folding by FOLD-TABLE.
  LAST-OP @ DUP IF
    DUP C@ FOLD-OP IF SWAP C! ELSE 2DROP EXIT-OP OP, THEN
  ELSE DROP EXIT-OP OP, THEN
  0 LAST-OP ! 0 STATE ! ?CSP REVEAL ; IMMEDIATE

\ BEGIN and DO make HERE a branch target without emitting anything
\ there, so the next primitive must not fuse with the one before.
\ (Folding never needed this: a BEGIN cannot come straight before `;`.)
: BEGIN8 ( --- a-addr )   0 LAST-OP ! HERE ; IMMEDIATE
: DO8 ( --- a-addr )
  POSTPONE (DO) 'LEAVE @ HERE 0 'LEAVE ! 0 LAST-OP ! ; IMMEDIATE

\ A test straight before IF, UNTIL or WHILE (which is IF) becomes one
\ fused branch, when SUPER-TABLE has (test, ?BRANCH, fused) - the
\ converter writes those first (Iteration 9: < for fib, 9% of its
\ dispatches). The test's byte is overwritten where it stands, so a
\ branch to it still lands on the fused one; LAST-OP's rules are
\ COMPILE,8's, and >MARK and <RESOLVE clear it after.
: ?BRANCH, ( --- )
  LAST-OP @ DUP IF DUP 1+ HERE = IF
    DUP C@ 0BRANCH-OP SUPER-OP IF SWAP C! EXIT THEN
  THEN THEN DROP 0BRANCH-OP OP, ;
: IF8 ( --- a-addr )   ?BRANCH, >MARK ; IMMEDIATE
: UNTIL8 ( a-addr --- )   ?BRANCH, <RESOLVE ; IMMEDIATE
